      "description": "Split Rock Lighthouse — located along the North Shore of Lake Superior, near Two Harbors, Minnesota.\n\nShipwrecks from a mighty 1905 November gale prompted this rugged landmark’s construction. Completed by the U.S. Lighthouse Service in 1910, Split Rock Light Station was soon one of Minnesota’s best known landmarks.\nRestored to its 1920s appearance, the lighthouse offers a glimpse of lighthouse life in this remote and spectacular setting.",
